---
title: Turkey, Black Bean, and Sweet Potato Chili
course: main
cuisine: tex-mex
servings: 4
time_active: 20
time_total: 55
leftovers: great
tags: [weeknight, one-pot, freezer-friendly]
description: Lean turkey chili with black beans and sweet potato, topped with Greek yogurt, cilantro, and lime.
---

Heat @olive oil{1%tbsp} in a #dutch oven{} over medium-high. Add @ground turkey{1%lb} and cook, breaking it up, until no longer pink, ~{5-6%minutes}.

Add a diced @yellow onion{1} and a pinch of @salt and cook until soft, ~{5%minutes}.

Stir in @garlic{3%clove}(minced), @chili powder{2%tbsp}, @cumin{2%tsp}, @smoked paprika{1%tsp}, @dried oregano{1%tsp}, and @tomato paste{2%tbsp}. Cook until the paste darkens, ~{2%minutes}.

Add @sweet potato{1}(large, peeled and cut into 1/2-inch cubes), @black beans{2%can}(15 oz, drained and rinsed), @diced tomatoes{1%can}(14.5 oz), and @chicken broth{2%cups}. Bring to a boil, then simmer partly covered until the sweet potato is tender and the chili has thickened, ~{30%minutes}.

Stir in the juice of half a @lime{1/2} and season with salt and @black pepper{}.

Serve topped with @?Greek yogurt{}, chopped @?cilantro{}, and wedges of @?lime{1}.

> Thickens overnight; loosen with a splash of water. Keeps 4 days, freezes up to 3 months.
